  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Harnessing the power of sports for impact investment and sustainable development outcomes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This workplan will champion sport for development and peace in Eastern Africa, building from the Kazan Action Plan and outcome documents and frameworks adopted at MINEPS VII, notably the Fit for Life Alliance and its Implementation Plan, further streamlined with the agreed approach of Sport in Africa to support Priority Africa, as well as the AU&#x2019;s 2023-2033 Policy Framework for Sustainable Development of Sport in Africa and the principles of the International Convention against Doping in Sport and of the International Charter of Physical Education, Physical Activity and Sport. This work will also leverage on relevant resources developed in the 41C/5 to further national step by step approaches for Fit for Life, harnessing impact investment while ensuring quality, integrity, inclusivity, and positive social transformations and lasting peace, powered by sport for a sustainable Eastern Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
